  "body": "<!-- strix-pr-review:master -->\n## Strix Security Review\n\n<!-- strix-pr-review:unreviewed-commits -->\n> [!WARNING]\n> This pull request has **1 commit** after the last Strix review (`ec93a00`). Strix has **not** reviewed these changes.\n> Automatic review on push is off for this repository. To review the latest changes, tag `@strix-security` in a comment, or [turn on re-review on push](https://app.strix.ai/repositories/60614550-3e9e-4537-af38-dcefce1735e3).\n<!-- /strix-pr-review:unreviewed-commits -->\n\nNo security issues found.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review summary</summary>\n\nThe diff only adds a replay marker (a boolean per-attempt `contextvar`, set and reset in `finally` on both the sync and async retry loops) and has the OpenAI provider build its per-attempt client with `with_options(max_retries=0)` when that marker is set. The client is copied rather than mutated, so the configured HTTP client/transport, credentials, base URL and default headers used by the interceptor path are preserved on every attempt, and no authentication, authorization, input-parsing, serialization, or output path is modified. No security issue found; static analysis on the two changed source files returned no findings. One non-security completeness observation: several OpenAI call sites (`responses.input_tokens.count`, the `with_raw_response.parse`/`with_raw_response.create` paths, and the beta `chat.completions.stream` helper) still use the raw client, so the retry-stacking reduction is only partial — worth folding into the same helper for consistency.\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>Updated for `ec93a00`.</sub>\n\n---\n*Reviewed by [Strix](https://strix.ai)*\n<sub>[Re-run review](https://app.strix.ai/api/pr-reviews/rerun?review_id=e2b32e21-5a05-47e0-b607-274a12330519) · [Configure security review settings](https://app.strix.ai/repositories/60614550-3e9e-4537-af38-dcefce1735e3)</sub>",
